messages.body:
**A list of what may not be called leaves out ROM routines that send any command.** IDF v5.4.1's `esp32s3.rom.ld` also provides:
- `SPI_Common_Command` (0x40000c90) and `spi_flash_hal_common_command` (0x40000d5c);
- `SPI_write_enable` (0x40000a44) and `spi_flash_common_write_status_16b_wrsr` (0x40000f0c);
- `spi_flash_attach` (0x40000aec) and `SPIMasterReadModeCnfig` (0x40000c84).

None of them is a "write or erase entry" by name. An allow-list of the ROM addresses the kernel may reference would hold without anyone having to choose the right entries. If the deny-list stays, give its by-address and jump-table forms a mutant each, beside the one by symbol.
